    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29777" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mōtōrĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		motor, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>moving, that has motion</i> (post-class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: modus agendi, <i>a stirring,
				bustling, noisy style of playing</i> (opp. statarius), Don.
				<i><span class="en">Ter. Ad. prol. 24</span></i>; id. ad argum. And.;
					<i><span class="en">Prisc. p. 590</span></i>
			P.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mōtōrĭum</span></b> ,
			ii, n., <i>the power of
				motion</i>, <i><span class="en">Tert. Anim.
		14</span></i>.</div>
